<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#mogho-naba">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mogho Naba</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Moro Naba, Mogho Naaba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mogho Naba ('ruler of the world') is the title of the king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mossi">Mossi</a> kingdom of Ouagadougou in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a>, the senior of the Mossi states. The office goes back several centuries, and its holder presides over a court of dignitaries and traditional ceremonies. Under French rule from 1896 the Mogho Naba kept ceremonial authority and was used to recruit labour, and the title remains influential today.</p></div>
